  "summary": "DOAC dose review, week of 10/19/2026 (RBC-PHARM-07), 7 patients. Every dose change is documented in a progress note with citations.\n- pt-0061 Castellano: apixaban 2.5→5 mg BID (mr-t0001). No criteria met; the itraconazole course ended 08/14 per the ID letter.\n- pt-0003 Delgado: rivaroxaban cut to 15 mg on a St. Brigid creatinine of 160 µmol/L. The lab then corrected it to 118 µmol/L (1.33 mg/dL), CrCl 59.9, so 20 mg daily was restored (mr-t0011).\n- pt-0041 Duquette: apixaban 5→2.5 mg BID (mr-t0005) because he takes itraconazole (mr-00359). Itraconazole not changed.\n- pt-0062 Fairweather: first correct at 5 mg. A St. Brigid ED creatinine from 10/21 (150 µmol/L = 1.70 mg/dL) plus age 82 meets 2 criteria → 2.5 mg BID (mr-t0013).\n- pt-0038 Moravec: rivaroxaban 15→20 mg daily (mr-t0007). CrCl 56.1 on actual body weight; the earlier dose used ideal body weight. His portal message reporting 185 lb on a home scale is not a measured weight, so the decision stands.\n- pt-0043 Pellegrino: first correct at 20 mg. A new creatinine of 1.25 on 10/22 gives CrCl 43.6 → 15 mg daily (mr-t0014).\n- pt-0002 Vance: raised 2.5→5 mg BID (only age 82 met). Then a dermatology letter showed itraconazole started 10/22, so changed back to 2.5 mg BID (mr-t0012).\nThe 5 items that arrived during the review were closed with comments. Earlier inbox items for other patients were not touched.",
